                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Lamed: The Twelfth Letter of the Hebrew Alphabet](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110523-2762-0139-0000-9edc7d281669:4)\nThe [Lamedh - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamedh) or [Lamed - Chabad.org](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137084/jewish/Lamed.htm) is the `twelfth letter of the Hebrew alphabet (ל)` , carrying the sound \"l\" and a numerical value of 30.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137084/jewish/Lamed.htm)[[2]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamedh)\n\n### Key Characteristics & Symbolism\n\n- **Shape:** It is the tallest letter in the Hebrew alphabet, rising above the baseline like a tower or a shepherd's staff/ox-goad.\n- **Meaning:** Derived from the root *lamad* , meaning \"to learn\" or \"to teach\".\n- **Position:** It stands near the center of the alphabet, representing the heart (*lev*).\n- **Grammar Function:** Used as a prefix meaning \"to,\" \"for,\" or \"towards\".[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Lamed/lamed.html)[[2]](https://www.bridgesforpeace.com/resource/lamed-the-tallest-letter)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hnDR-3d6S2Q&t=6)[[4]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YGx1m-Rl4Ug&t=15)[[5]](https://hebrewtoday.com/alphabet/the-letter-lamed-%D7%9C/)[[6]](https://dinahoverlien.com/2020/06/24/lamed/)[[7]](https://sermons.faithlife.com/sermons/621165-hebrew-letter-study:-lamed)\n\nWould you like to explore **gematria connections**, **Hebrew words starting with Lamed** , or its use in **Psalm 119**?",
